   "sentenceId": 13,
   "he": "וְלֹא זֶה וָזֶה זַכָּאִין בִּמְצִיאָתָהּ וְכוּ׳. טַעְמָא מַאי אֲמוּר רַבָּנַן מְצִיאַת אִשָּׁה לְבַעְלָהּ — כִּי הֵיכִי דְּלָא תִּיהְוֵי לֵיהּ אֵיבָה. הָכָא תִּיהְוֵי לֵיהּ אֵיבָה וְאֵיבָה.",
   "en": "§ The mishna further taught: «Neither this one nor that one is entitled to her found» articles. The Gemara explains: «What is the reason» that «the Sages said» that the «found» object «of a wife» belongs «to her husband? So that he should not harbor enmity» toward her, due to her refusal to give him the item she found. «Here,» however, «let him harbor much enmity» toward her, as the Sages want him to divorce her."
  }
